<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Guzmán Fernández</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a>–<a href="/years/1982">1982</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Guzmán Fernández was President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> from 1978 to 1982 for the Dominican Revolutionary Party. His election victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joaquin-balaguer">Joaquín Balaguer</a> in 1978, upheld after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> pressure stopped the army from halting the count, brought the country's first peaceful transfer of power between parties. He freed political prisoners and curbed the military, but shot himself in the last weeks of his term.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-guzman-fernandez.jpg" alt="Antonio Guzmán Fernández" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fotograf%C3%ADa_oficial_del_presidente_D._Antonio_Guzm%C3%A1n_(2)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
